From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:04:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: give E and P cores their measured
 capacity

Without capacity-dmips-mhz every T8132 core reports capacity 1024, so the
scheduler treats the Donan E cores as equals of the P cores and places
latency-sensitive work (Hyprland frame composition on J713) on them.

Measured on a J713 (M4 MacBook Air) running cpufreq with schedutil, E at
2892 MHz and P at 4104 MHz (cpuinfo maxima): twelve single-threaded
programs (gcc -O2, zstd -19, bzip2 -9, gzip -9, xz -6, zlib, node,
sqlite, perl, lua and two CPython loops), each pinned and run three times
on two cores per cluster. The E/P wall-time ratio has a geometric mean of
0.519 (0.39 to 0.67), the same on battery and on AC. arch_topology scales
capacity-dmips-mhz by each cluster's maximum frequency, so
E = 0.519 * 4104 / 2892 * 1024 = 754, giving E cores a capacity of 531.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 00f3d79440108554a65fd196ec8b8b9fec5e5268)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 7eb1ecb1d9..75b75a1038 100644
